<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ s/adj production GDP rises 0.6 pct in Sept qtr.</title>
<headline>NZ s/adj production GDP rises 0.6 pct in Sept qtr.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics New Zealand on Thursday released the following estimates of New Zealand's real, production-based gross domestic product for the quarter ended Sept 30, 1996.</p>
<p>Thirteen economists polled by Reuters expected on average a 0.21 percent real, seasonally adjusted rise in the quarter, for a 1.72 percent real s/adj rise between the September 1995 and September 1996 quarters, and a 2.25 percent actual annual rise.</p>
<p>Quarter-on-quarter seasonally-adjusted figures (revised-from figures in brackets):</p>
<p>    Sept 1996		  June 1996		  Sept 1995</p>
<p>    0.6 pct		    0.3 pct		    0.4 pct (0.5)</p>
<p>S/adj change at constant prices from yr-ago quarter</p>
<p>    Sept 1996		  June 1996		  Sept 1995</p>
<p>    2.2 pct		    2.0 pct (2.1)	    3.1 pct (3.2)</p>
<p>Actual annual change</p>
<p>    Sept 1996		  June 1996		  Sept 1995</p>
<p>    2.3 pct		    2.5 pct (2.6)	    4.3 pct</p>
<p>Quarterly contributions to GDP movements (percent)</p>
<p>				  Sept 1996	   June 1996</p>
<p>    Agriculture		   -1.3		 0.2</p>
<p>    Fishing, forestry, mining  6.4		-0.2</p>
<p>    Manufacturing		  1.7		-0.5</p>
<p>    Power, gas, water	   -2.6		-0.7</p>
<p>    Construction		  -0.7		-0.5</p>
<p>    Restaurants, hotels	  1.0		 0.7</p>
<p>    Dwellings			0.4		 0.4</p>
<p>    Transport, Communications  1.6		 0.7</p>
<p>    Govt services		 -0.3		-0.3</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 473-4746</p>
</text>
